    {
      "id": "2178830d-f5d6-46a1-9cba-6352afba8187",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 283,
      "shortId": "PNC8T",
      "priority": 6,
      "shortName": "choice-6-propvalue-list-grid-r",
      "title": "choice-6: `PropValue::List` + `Grid` realize (tracks, areas, placement)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "`Grid` is the **only** kind left that genuinely needs a structured prop. Add the one model primitive it needs and realize it.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-14 — heca 348, heca-grid-ui 140, clippy clean, user tested the showcase.\n\n## Shipped\n- **`PropValue::List(Vec<PropValue>)`** (`view.rs`) — one new variant, the **last** the phase needs. Its rustdoc says why it is rare: the option-shaped widgets do NOT use it (their options are **children** — an option is a node with a value and content, not a string). Covered by a JSON round-trip test over the whole `PropValue` vocabulary, nested list included (the WASM boundary).\n- **`Grid` realize arm** — `columns` / `rows` / `areas` as lists; **placement is a prop on the CHILD** (`area` by name, or `col`/`row` + optional spans, defaulting to 1). Neither → taffy auto-placement; an unknown area name → auto-placement too. Keeps `ViewNode`'s shape flat.\n- **`parse_track()`** — CSS-like strings (`\"22px\"` / bare number / `\"1fr\"` / `\"auto\"` / `\"min\"`(`-content`) / `\"max\"`(`-content`)), case-insensitive + trimmed. **Anything unrecognised degrades to `Auto`** — never a panic (untrusted input).\n- **`Grid::area_boxed` / `cell_boxed`** — the boxed-setter seam (`Dialog::body_boxed` precedent).\n\n## Follow-up from the user's test (same task)\nThe showcase Grid demo exposed **two real gaps**, both now closed:\n\n1. **A grid item is pinned to the TOP-LEFT of its cell by default.** `Stretch` on both axes + an explicitly-sized item (every leaf has one — a `Label` measures to `font × 1.4`, an `Icon` to `font`) = nothing to stretch, so it lands at the cell start. An `Icon` and a `Label` in one row do NOT share a centre line. The vertical knob (`align`) existed; the **horizontal one did not** — and `justify` is a trap: on a grid it is `justify-content`, which distributes the whole *track set* and never moves an item in its cell. **Added `Style::justify_items` / `Style::justify_self` + the `LayoutExt` builders**, wired into `to_taffy`. `realize` now reads `align` + `justify_items` on a `Grid`, and **`align_self` / `justify_self` on EVERY kind** (they describe a node inside its parent, so they are read centrally in `realize`, not per arm).\n2. **The `areas` template defines the structure; `rows`/`columns` only *size* the tracks it implies.** A template with more lines than row tracks silently creates **implicit** rows — and an item spanning them is centred over a taller area than its neighbours, which reads as \"the text is off-centre\". This bit the user immediately when they wrote a 1-row grid but left a 2-line template. Documented with a WRONG/RIGHT pair; rule of thumb: **count the lines in `areas` — that is how many rows you have.**\n\n## Tests (heca 348 · heca-grid-ui 140)\nGrid: `grid_tracks_parse_and_garbage_degrades_to_auto` · `grid_node_realizes_tracks_areas_and_per_child_placement` · `grid_child_in_an_unknown_area_auto_places` · `grid_alignment_is_authorable_on_both_axes` · `every_prop_value_round_trips_including_lists` · **`grid_items_align_in_their_cell_on_both_axes`** (the top-left default; `align` centres vertically; `justify_items` horizontally; the per-item overrides win; and `justify` deliberately does **not** move an item — the trap, pinned) · **`grid_areas_template_defines_the_rows_not_the_row_tracks`** (a one-line template shares a centre line; a two-line template with the same single row track does not).\n\n## Showcase\n`Grid` had **no** demo at all (an AGENTS requirement). Added two: the two-row rich row (icon spanning both lines, `align: Center`, dot pinned right with `justify_self`), and the single-line variant that shows the one-line-template rule. The *declarative* path cannot be shown there — `realize` is app-side (`heca`), and `heca-renderer` does not depend on `heca`.\n\n## Docs\n`docs/widgets.md` `Grid` entry: Native + Declarative examples; the full track vocabulary + degrade rule; **\"The `areas` template defines the structure\"** (WRONG/RIGHT pair); **\"Aligning items inside their cells (read this — the default surprises people)\"** — the four-knob table (align / justify_items / align_self / justify_self), the `justify` trap, and examples per axis. `LayoutExt` table + the model table updated. `view.rs` rustdoc in sync.\n\n## Gates\nclippy 0 warnings · heca **348** · heca-grid-ui **140** + 71 + 1 · showcase builds. No `cargo fmt`.",
