    {
      "id": "af69ae20-58d6-4014-a4b7-9294e0c7ebe1",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 285,
      "shortId": "S4SSC",
      "priority": 8,
      "shortName": "choice-8-vocabulary-coverage-p",
      "title": "choice-8 vocabulary coverage plus Choice vs Item guidance",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "The closing task: make the \"not realized yet\" list **empty by construction**, and write the `Choice` vs `Item` guidance.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-14 — workspace green (heca 354 · heca-grid-ui 142 · heca-core 89 · …), clippy 0. Docs-and-guard work; **no UI surface to test**.\n\n## 1. The coverage guard (the point of the task)\n`every_widget_kind_realizes_to_a_live_widget_except_the_host_only_ones` walks **`WidgetKind::ALL`**, realizes a representative node per kind, lays it out and paints it, and asserts the result is **alive** — it either holds the children it was given or paints something. The empty-`Flex` fallback does *neither*, so **a kind with no `realize` arm fails loudly** instead of rendering nothing and being discovered months later by a plugin author. That failure mode is invisible in review and invisible at runtime; this is the only thing that catches it.\n\n**Two layers stop the guard itself from rotting** (a guard is only as good as the list it walks):\n- `sample_node(kind)`'s match is **exhaustive** → a new `WidgetKind` **fails to compile** until it has a sample.\n- `WidgetKind::ordinal()` is exhaustive too, and `all_lists_every_widget_kind` ties it to `ALL` → a variant that reaches `ordinal` but not `ALL` **fails the test**.\n\n`ScrollBar` is asserted to realize to **nothing** — so the host-only decision is *pinned by a test*, not merely documented.\n\n## 2. `ScrollBar` — host-only, and the rule generalized\n`realize` keeps it out of the realized set and its debug log now says why (\"its state is a live host signal, which static data cannot drive — use Scroll\"). Documented as a **general principle**, not a one-off:\n\n> **A widget whose state is a live host signal is HOST-ONLY.**\n\nA `ViewNode` is static, serializable data: it cannot carry a signal, let alone update one, so a declarative `ScrollBar` would render a **dead control** (a thumb that never moves). Plugins use **`Scroll`** (a `ScrollRegion`), which owns its own offset. The rule also covers individual **builders** — `DockFrame::rail(..)` binds a host-owned `RegionMode` signal, so a declarative dock is never rail-aware.\n\n## 3. `Choice` vs `Item` guidance\nThe comparison table + rule of thumb (from choice-1) is now **cross-referenced from both entries** — the `Item` entry gained a callout (\"Both are selectable, both compose their content, both are one Tab stop — but they answer different questions\"), pointing at the full table. `Item` = a **row** (leading · label · trailing, fixed height, `ActiveMarker`) — a list that looks like rows. `Choice` = **any content + a value** — the user is picking one of several.\n\n## 4. Docs sweep — every stale claim gone\n- `realize.rs` module rustdoc: \"arms are filled in incrementally … unhandled kinds fall back to an empty container\" → a **Coverage** section (complete; the host-only exception; and *the test that enforces it*).\n- `view.rs`: `WidgetKind::ALL` + `ordinal` with the guard explained; the props/events table carries every kind.\n- `docs/widgets.md`: the \"not realized yet\" list is **gone**, replaced by a coverage statement; `ScrollBar` gained a **host-only** callout (why a declarative one would be a dead control, use `Scroll` instead, and the general rule); the last `viewnode-task-1` reference (Item's slots) now points at Named child slots.\n- `docs/chrome-and-ui.md`: closed-vocabulary section states **every `WidgetKind` is authorable**, with the host-only exception and *why* it generalizes.\n- **AGENTS.md ⭐ block**: \"Genuinely OPEN\" no longer lists realize coverage (it is complete) — the remaining open items are a typed builder SDK over `ViewNode` and `Label` truncation/wrapping. The **SETTLED** list now records: coverage is complete *and test-enforced*; composition; options-as-children + value→intent; the `slot` prop; content-color inheritance; and the host-only rule.\n\n## Gates\nclippy `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings · `cargo test --workspace` green (heca **354**, heca-grid-ui 142 + 71 + 1, heca-core 89, …) · showcase builds. No `cargo fmt`.\n\n## PHASE COMPLETE\nchoice-1..8 all done. `ViewNode` coverage is closed: every `WidgetKind` realizes, enforced by a test.",
      "notes": "",
