      "phaseId": "f9a8c93b-6938-4644-88e4-f1d2d2f59d6d",
      "number": 286,
      "shortId": "QPPAW",
      "priority": 9,
      "shortName": "gridui-debt-dialog-font-derive",
      "title": "gridui-debt Dialog font-derived min-width needs Style min_width",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "**Rescued from the old root `HANDOFF.md` §3c (deleted 2026-07-13); do not lose this.**\n\nA short confirm dialog (\"Delete Pane?\") renders **cramped** — the panel hugs its content, so a two-word title + two buttons produces a tiny box, and dialogs of different content have visibly different widths with no shared baseline.\n\n## The gap\n`Style` (`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs`) has **no `min_width`** — only `width`/`height` (`Length::{Auto, Px}`). So `Dialog` cannot express \"hug the content, but never below a sensible floor\".\n\n## Work\n1. Add `min_width: Length` (and probably `min_height` for symmetry — decide) to `Style`, defaulting to `Length::Auto`, and wire it into `Style::to_taffy()` (taffy has `min_size`). Add the builder to `LayoutExt`.\n2. Give `Dialog`'s panel a **font-derived** minimum — the note said **~22em** (i.e. `22 × base font`), so it scales with the theme font instead of being a magic pixel count. Verify against the real dialogs (delete-pane confirm, the rename form).\n3. Tests: a `min_width` smaller than the content is a no-op; larger than the content floors the box; it scales with the base font.\n4. `docs/widgets.md`: the `Style`/`LayoutExt` tables + the `Dialog` entry.\n\n## Why it's here\n`gridui-07` (crate-review debt) is the right home: it is a missing primitive in the layout style, not a feature.\n\n## Gates\nclippy 0; `cargo test -p heca-grid-ui -p heca`; showcase green; no `cargo fmt`.",
