    {
      "id": "bc9ca992-57d9-4c4b-bc19-b92fa948d1f9",
      "phaseId": "8f760a9b-3ce8-4932-8286-67d742397f2e",
      "number": 287,
      "shortId": "BL773",
      "priority": 8,
      "shortName": "context-menu-bug-keyboard-navi",
      "title": "context-menu-bug keyboard navigation of an open menu does nothing",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "**BUG, rescued from the old root `HANDOFF.md` §3c (deleted 2026-07-13); do not lose this.**\n\nThe user reported that **`Ctrl+j`/`Ctrl+k` and the arrow keys do not navigate an open context menu** — the highlight does not move.\n\n## What was already checked (the code path *traces* correct)\n1. `top_modal(state)` matches while the menu is open, so the overlay-capture gate in `route_interaction` blocks WM actions — that part works.\n2. The **widget keymap** path delivers the key (`heca/src/app/events.rs`, overlay key branch → `Keymap::dispatch`).\n3. `ContextMenu::event` returns `Handled::No` on a **raw** arrow, which is what lets the host resolve it into the semantic `WidgetIntent::{MenuUp, MenuDown}` and re-deliver it.\n4. `input_mode` is reset to `Normal` at `heca/src/input.rs:229`.\n\nSo the trace looks right and the bug is **not** where it was expected. **It needs a runtime repro.**\n\n## Prime suspects (from the note)\n- The **`[keys.widgets]` defaults** — are `menu_up`/`menu_down` actually bound to `↑`/`Ctrl+k` and `↓`/`Ctrl+j` in `keybindings.default.toml`, and does `build_widget_keymap` pick them up?\n- The **`>` shifted-binding match** — a shifted-symbol binding may be swallowing or mis-resolving the combo before the menu ever sees it.\n\n## How to work it\nReproduce in the running app: open a context menu, press the keys, and instrument the four trace points above to see which one does not fire. Do **NOT** attempt a fix from the code trace alone — that is exactly what already failed once.\n\n## Gates\nclippy 0; `cargo test -p heca`; the user confirms the menu navigates in the real app; no `cargo fmt`.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nCHIUSO 2026-07-14 — il bug NON esiste più. L'utente ha confermato a runtime: \"ctrl+j/k for me is fixed\".\n\nVERIFICA DEL CODICE (i due \"prime suspects\" della nota sono entrambi PULITI):\n1. `[keys.widgets]` (keybindings.default.toml:221-226): `menu_up = [\"ArrowUp\",\"Ctrl+k\"]`, `menu_down = [\"ArrowDown\",\"Ctrl+j\"]` — presenti e corretti.\n2. `build_widget_keymap` (heca/src/app/registry.rs:135) mappa `menu_up`/`menu_down` → `WidgetIntent::MenuUp`/`MenuDown` leggendo la config.\n3. `ContextMenu::event` (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/context_menu.rs:463): su `Event::Widget(MenuDown/MenuUp)` chiama `select_next`/`select_prev` → l'highlight si muove. I tasti RAW non vengono ingoiati (`Handled::No`), così l'host può risolverli in `WidgetIntent` e ri-consegnarli.\nNessun binding shiftato (`>`) intercetta la combo.\n\nCAUSA PROBABILE DELLA GUARIGIONE: commit 8f55108 \"feat(app): overlay-capture interaction policy…\", che ha toccato il ramo overlay dei tasti in `app/events.rs` (il punto di consegna). Il bug era stato aperto PRIMA di quel commit.\n\nPERCHÉ ERA POSSIBILE ROMPERLO IN SILENZIO (e perché nessuno sapeva dire quando fosse tornato a funzionare): la metà WIDGET della catena non era coperta da NESSUN test. La metà host sì (`widget_keymap_maps_default_bindings_by_axis` in app/registry.rs già asseriva Ctrl+j→MenuDown, Ctrl+k→MenuUp).\n\nREGRESSION TEST AGGIUNTI (è questo il vero deliverable del task):\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/context_menu.rs::menu_intents_move_the_highlight_and_skip_disabled_entries` — dato l'intent semantico, la selezione SI MUOVE, salta le voci disabilitate, non wrappa agli estremi, e un tasto RAW resta `Handled::No` (se lo ingoiasse, la navigazione si romperebbe di nuovo: è esattamente il modo in cui questo bug può tornare).\n- `heca/src/app/registry.rs::widget_keymap_maps_default_bindings_by_axis` — aggiunta l'asserzione mancante `ArrowUp → MenuUp` (c'erano già ArrowDown/Ctrl+j/Ctrl+k).\n\nNON TESTABILE IN UNIT TEST: il ramo di consegna in `app/events.rs` (richiede AppState + finestra reale). Resta coperto solo dalla verifica manuale dell'utente.\n\nGATE: clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features 0 warning; heca 361 + heca-grid-ui 72 (era 71) verdi.",
